c Format reference: https://github.com/crillab/d4

c o, for an OR node
c f, for a false leaf
c t, for a true leaf
c a, for an AND node

c The second argument just after the type of node is its index.

c In the example the decision-DNNF representation has
c 3 OR nodes (1, 2 and 3) and 1 true node (4).

o 1 0
o 2 0
o 3 0
t 4 0
3 4 -2 3 0
3 4 2 0
2 3 -1 0
2 4 1 0
1 2 0

c In the example, 3 4 -2 3 0 means that OR node of index 3 is connected to the
c true node of index 4 and the literals -2 and 3 are set to true.
